NAME
       pidof - print the process IDs of a running program

SYNOPSIS
       pidof PROGRAM...

DESCRIPTION
       pidof prints, on one line, the PIDs of the processes running the
       named programs. The name must match exactly (no patterns). It exits
       with 0 when it found something and 1 when not. pgrep is more
       flexible.

EXAMPLES
           pidof sshd
           kill $(pidof sleep)

SEE ALSO
       pgrep(1), ps(1), kill(1)
